// A for-in over a value that is not a List, String, Map, or Coroutine is a
// halting fault (spec/04-semantics.md, Halting Faults). The fault must occur:
// the loop body and the code after the loop never run, and the program exits
// with a non-zero status.
for (var x in 5) { print x; }
print "after";

// STATUS: error
